Understanding Log Data

Logs are records of events within an organization's systems and networks, crucial for security analysis.
Common log sources include firewall logs (recording internet traffic), network logs (tracking device connections), and server logs (detailing service-related events like logins).
The Role of SIEM Tools 

SIEM tools collect and analyze log data to monitor critical activities, providing real-time visibility and automated alerts.
These tools centralize log data, increasing efficiency by minimizing the need for manual review and analysis by security professionals.
  
